BUNDLED BOOT ARTIFACTS

THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES.md is generated from pnpm-lock.yaml and so covers npm
dependencies only. The boot artifacts below are built from upstream source or
redistributed as upstream release binaries, and are attributed here instead.

1. GNU GRUB, GPL-3.0-or-later

   Bootloader images the bridge serves to devices booting from local disk:
   apps/bridge/assets/download/grub/bootx64.efi, bootaa64.efi and core.img.
   Upstream: https://www.gnu.org/software/grub/

   Built from the Ubuntu 24.04 (noble) grub-common, grub-efi-amd64-bin,
   grub-efi-arm64-bin and grub-pc-bin packages; the EFI images report GRUB
   2.12-1ubuntu7.3. GRUB's own source is not modified. grub-mkstandalone packs
   the distribution's stock modules and embeds one of our configuration files
   as boot/grub/grub.cfg. Those configuration files are in
   apps/bridge/boot/grub/ and the build recipe is
   apps/local-sim/scripts/local/grub-build.sh.

2. iPXE, GPL-2.0-or-later

   Network-boot firmware (ipxe.efi, snp.efi, snponly.efi and an ipxe.iso)
   built into the bridge container image. The binaries are not committed to
   this repository. Upstream: https://github.com/ipxe/ipxe, pinned at commit
   5921e6b45.

   Most iPXE files additionally offer the Unmodified Binary Distribution
   Licence (COPYING.UBDL) as an alternative to the GPL. The builds distributed
   here include files declared FILE_LICENCE ( GPL2_OR_LATER ) without that
   alternative, among them interface/efi/efi_path.c and net/ipmi_settings.c,
   so the UBDL is not available for these binaries and they are conveyed under
   the GPL.

   iPXE is modified. apps/bridge/boot/ipxe/ is copied over the upstream tree
   before the build: overlay/ carries our source changes and additions (IPMI
   transports and settings, EFI device paths, DNS, the root certificate
   store), config/general.h and config/branding.h override feature selection
   and branding, and autoexec-chainload.ipxe is embedded into the firmware.

3. curl, curl license (an MIT/X derivative)

   Static curl binaries packed into the brokkr-live initrd (brokkr-live.img):
   apps/bridge/boot/initrd-live/usr/bin/curl-amd64 and curl-arm64.
   Redistributed unmodified from release v8.11.0 of
   https://github.com/moparisthebest/static-curl; the exact download URLs are
   recorded in apps/bridge/boot/initrd-live/usr/bin/README. Upstream curl:
   https://curl.se/

   Both are curl 8.11.0 linked statically against musl libc, OpenSSL, zlib,
   nghttp2 and libssh2. The amd64 binary reports OpenSSL 3.1.7 (Apache-2.0);
   the arm64 binary reports OpenSSL 1.1.1t (dual OpenSSL/SSLeay license).
   musl libc and nghttp2 are MIT, zlib is under the zlib license, and libssh2
   is BSD-3-Clause. None of these components is copyleft.

